SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Katonisiotissa\, Kato Nisi
LOCATION:Kato Nisi\, Elafonisos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's big day: an all-night vigil at the church of Panagia Katonisiotissa in Kato Nisi on the 14th\, while the young people light fires on the Panagia beach below and sing and dance until dawn\; liturgy on the morning of the 15th\, then a popular panigiri with the island's women's and children's dance groups in the afternoon. Boats used to bring crowds from Mani and Kythira\; today it is islanders and summer visitors\, and the beach bonfire is the thing to see.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/elafonisos/#kato-nisi-panigiri-of-panagia-katonisiotissa-kato-nisi
